From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: misc: hy310-board-mgr: the lamp as bl0, set with the fan's modes

The L018's stock fan driver owns the lamp as well (pwm_fan.c, read off
the stock kernel, 25.10.2026): with fan_policy 1 one mode index sets the
fan's duty-array-policy1 and the lamp's bl0 duty-array, and the
temperature does not drive the fan. Above temp_warn for more than 30
cycles of 2 s it switches to mode 3, which dims the lamp, keeps the
chosen mode and restores it at temp_resume.

This driver now does the same where a tree asks for it:

- A bl0 subnode with duty-array (and dft_period_ns, else the fans'
  pwm_period_ns) and a PWM named "bl0" give the driver the lamp. Every
  mode change (probe, cooling device, resume) sets fans and lamp from the
  same index; the lamp's PWM is never disabled.
- lamp-mode-names in bl0 names the modes a user may choose. sysfs
  lamp_mode (read: the chosen mode, write: a name), lamp_modes (the
  names) and thermal_mode (1 while the thermal mode holds); the
  attributes exist only with a lamp.
- thermal-mode = <index> together with temp_resume: after NTC_WARN_CYCLES
  above temp_warn the driver sets that index instead of forcing every fan
  to 100 %, keeps the chosen mode, and sets it again once the NTC reads
  temp_resume or less. A mode chosen meanwhile is kept for then, so the
  lamp does not get brighter while the box is hot.

A tree without bl0 - the HY310, both HY300 Pro trees, the HY200 trees -
takes none of these paths: no lamp, no attributes, the overtemp action
stays "all fans 100 %". Only the L018 tree (0331) has a bl0 node.

Built in the h713-build container (drivers/misc/hy310-board-mgr.o, W=1:
no compiler warning). Measured on the L018, 25.10.2026: the probe logs
"bl0: lamp on PWM bl0, 4 modes, 3 by name" and "thermal mode 3 above
41 C, back at 34 C"; lamp_mode low/std/high give PWM2 720/480/288 and
PWM0 576/672/912 of 960 cycles - the registers the stock firmware wrote
in the same three modes (24.10.2026) - and the fan follows (2880/3210
rpm at low/std). The thermal mode itself is not measured (the NTC read
21 C). Not run on the other boards: their trees have no bl0, which the
code paths above were read for.

